  "claim_boundary": "This is a strengthened world-seed-0 development qualification for task readiness and one shared public-history-only hybrid participant scaffold. It retains the v0.2 keyed observation-noise namespace so v1.6-to-v1.7 development comparisons use the same observation realization rather than selecting a new noise trial. Random search and Latin-hypercube sampling remain difficulty controls and are not counted as adaptive capability families. Public surrogate candidate generation does not use hidden world fields and does not itself commit a recipe; the model selects every recipe after experiment eight. This qualification cannot establish multi-world robustness, method superiority, provider effects, or publication-grade effect sizes. Failure cannot be repaired by lowering a frozen task threshold post hoc."
